      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Katherine, this sysprop is used by android team for qualification only (under packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/bta/av/bta_av_aact.cc).\n\nI didn\u0027t see them put this in the system/libsysprop and system/sepolicy so I guess they intend to do it because there\u0027s no other use cases for this sysprop.\n\nMay I know if there are reasons that we need to add them in system/libsysprop and system/sepolicy? \n\nAndroid team uses this sysprop through the command \"adb shell setprop bluetooth.pts.force_a2dp_abort true\" (from tools/test/connectivity/acts_tests/tests/google/bt/pts/instructions/AVDTP_PTS_INSTUCTIONS) for qualification used.\n\nAnd for chromeos, we can use this sysprop by appending \"bluetooth.pts.force_a2dp_abort\u003dtrue\" at the end of the file /var/lib/bluetooth/sysprops.conf.",
      "parentUuid": "789fecd9_700f9826",
